/T (This devotion has deep roots in the Church's history. Following the Battle of Lepanto on 7th  October 1571, Pope Pius V attributed a remarkable victory to the prayers of the faithful who had turned to the Rosary. Since then, generations of Catholics have treasured it as a source of strength, hope, and peace. In 2002, Pope St. John Paul II renewed its importance by introducing the Luminous Mysteries, helping us contemplate Christ's public ministry and his gift of the Eucharist.)
