<<
/Title (This devotion has deep roots in the Church's history. Following the Battle of Lepanto on 7th  October 1571, Pope Pius V attributed a remarkable victory to the prayers of the faithful who had turned to the Rosary. Since then, generations of Catholics have treasured it as a source of strength, hope, and peace. In 2002, Pope St. John Paul II renewed its importance by introducing the Luminous Mysteries, helping us contemplate Christ's public ministry and his gift of the Eucharist.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 312 0 R
/Prev 559 0 R
/Next 576 0 R
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Rosary is a prayer of both heart and mind. As our fingers move gently from bead to bead, our thoughts rest on the mysteries of Christ's life, death, and resurrection. Through the Joyful, Luminous, Sorrowful, and Glorious Mysteries, we journey through the Gospel itself, seeing the face of Christ through Mary's eyes.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 312 0 R
/Prev 575 0 R
/Next 560 0 R
>>
endobj
